# Conformance probe pack for rulings 17, 18, 25 and 27 of spec 0.8, most
# significant bit first. Public. Three kinds, told apart by byte 2.
#
#   byte 0      n
#   byte 1      presence p.1 and p.2, then 6 unused bits
#   byte 2      1: kind a    2: kind b    3: kind c
#   kind a      x in 8 bits unless p.2 is 1; then z in 8 bits
#   kind b      p.1: y in 8 bits; then a count in 8 bits and that many recs.
#               Every item starts with the nibble 9, then a nibble that
#               selects its kind: 1 point (y in 8 bits), 0 empty
#   kind c      a count in 8 bits and that many nums; an item is val in 8
#               bits when p.1 is 1, and no bits at all when it is 0
#
# p.1 is named only in kinds b and c, and p.2 only with `!` in kind a: both
# are bits an `if` block names, in every kind (ruling 17). The `when` of kind
# a stands after its `requires` and `default` lines (ruling 18). The `when`
# before the first `kind` of the recs body is common to every item (ruling 27).
format     conformance-seq-rulings-kinds
version    0.8.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
layout     sequential
bit_order  msb
field   probe.n  8  uint
presence p 2
pad 6
kind    a
requires probe.x
default probe.z  3
when    8  1
if !p.2
  field  probe.x  8  uint
end
field   probe.z  8  uint
kind    b
when    8  2
if p.1
  field  probe.y  8  uint
end
group   probe.recs count 8
  when   4  9
  kind   point
  when   4  1
  requires probe.y
  field  probe.y  8  uint
  kind   empty
  when   4  0
end
kind    c
when    8  3
group   probe.nums count 8
  if p.1
    field  probe.val  8  uint
  end
end
